@startuml managed-file-states
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
title One managed file at start-up (reconcile.rs, "reconcile a file")

state "Read" as Read #DDEBF7 : fs.read(path)
state "Valid" as Valid #EDEDED : passes its check:\nnever written
state "Missing" as Missing #EDEDED
state "Damaged" as Damaged #F8CBAD : fails its check
state "Backed up" as BackedUp #FCE4D6 : a durable copy in\n<root>/backups/<session>/
state "Repaired" as Repaired #FCE4D6 : its usable part or its default,\nrenamed over it (write_atomic)
state "Created" as Created #FCE4D6 : its default, published without\nreplacing anything (write_new)
state "Absent" as Absent #EDEDED : left to its owner
state "Left as it is" as Blocked #EDEDED : reported; nothing is saved\nto it this session

[*] --> Read
Read --> Valid : the check passes
Read --> Damaged : the check fails
Read --> Missing : not found
Read --> Blocked : unreadable, a link to nothing,\nor a newer format
Missing --> Created : it has a default:\nsettings, examples,\nuser-id, state files
Missing --> Absent : no default: lists, grants,\nfreshness; the marker is step 4's
Missing --> Read : write_new finds something\nappeared meanwhile: look once more
Damaged --> BackedUp : Backups::copy_into:\ncreate, sync the file, sync the folder
Damaged --> Blocked : the copy fails:\nnever repaired without one
BackedUp --> Repaired : temporary file, sync,\nrename over, sync the folder
BackedUp --> Absent : wallet-active only:\nremove, sync the folder
Valid --> [*]
Repaired --> [*]
Created --> [*]
Absent --> [*]
Blocked --> [*]

note right of BackedUp #F8CBAD
  **A crash before the rename:** the file still holds its
  original, and the next start makes a new copy.
  **A crash after it:** the file holds its whole repair.
  So the file is never absent, and its content is never
  only in a backup (the model's NeverAbsent, RepairInPlace).
end note

note left of Valid
  A second start finds every file Valid,
  Created or Absent: it writes nothing
  but its busy flag.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#DDEBF7> | F1R3Gaze reads the file |
  |<#F8CBAD> | damage, and crashes |
  |<#FCE4D6> | a durable write |
  |<#EDEDED> | nothing is written |
endlegend
@enduml
